## UX scope and remaining work

The tested policy retains the reviewed source-set/root/nonroot naming rules,
null-versus-empty distinction, unknown-versus-non-Gradle distinction, and separate
display/holder/sort identities. It preserves imported names, reported paths,
Unicode, whitespace, delimiters, and collision suffixes without filesystem or
folder guesses. Empty labels are preserved instead of silently normalized.

An authoritative getter/import identity producer, imported name construction,
holder lookup, Kotlin facet/capability producer, revision-bound publication,
project-panel wiring, and adapter support for empty labels remain absent.
There is no new user-visible naming workflow or live tree screenshot proved
by these component tests. The five original generated-tree methods and original
Kotlin tests remain unported/not_run; **new original-reference parity credit is
zero**. This addendum does not certify full app build, native/live UX,
full-workspace tests, full CI, protected integration, phase completion, or IDE
completion. Those remain pending lead integration gates.

This reviewer ran no executable, Cargo, Gradle, app, compiler, SDK probe, or
cache operation, and changed no repository source, fixture, matrix, main, or
protected branch. Only external review evidence was written.
